From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:43:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] The release decider says the routes its draw now decides

`pro.release`'s stream goes on past the late, streaming and shelved shares into `routeOf` since the routes were built, so
its description listing only those three stopped being the whole of what the draw decides.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HBdcuKzBBMbipfFQSByALG
---
 src/engine/decided.ts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/engine/decided.ts b/src/engine/decided.ts
index e4b02570..8b25242c 100644
--- a/src/engine/decided.ts
+++ b/src/engine/decided.ts
@@ -897,7 +897,7 @@ defineDecider<{ sim: Simulation; first: number }, string>({
 
 defineDecider<{ sim: Simulation; first: number; after: number }, string>({
   id: 'pro.release',
-  decides: 'A slate production’s way out after the wrap (RELEASE_FATE): on time, held back months, sent to streaming instead of cinemas, or shelved, by the way its format comes out.',
+  decides: 'A slate production’s way out after the wrap (RELEASE_FATE): on time, held back months, sent to streaming instead of cinemas, or shelved, and from 2026-10-25 a limited release, another distributor’s later date or a film abroad first (routeOf), by the way its format comes out.',
   drawnIn: 'src/engine/systems/projobs.ts',
   reads: {
     first: (o, t) => ({ ...o, first: Math.round(t * 100) }),
